# Template — see tofu/tailscale/secrets.sops.env.example for the procedure and for why the
# pass:// line below carries no braces.
#
# Only this module's own credential lives here. Everything else it needs — the node address, the
# tailnet suffix, the internal base domain — is owned by another plane, so it is declared in
# refs.env and read from that plane's file at plan/apply time instead of copied here.
#
# Anything named here WINS over refs.env, because `sops exec-env` runs after the refs are
# exported. A value present in both places is not a harmless duplicate: it silently disables the
# ref, which is exactly how this file came to hold a stale second copy of the node address.
BUNNYNET_API_KEY=pass://futharkd/bunny/api key
